  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1073,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 1089,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 152561,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 155,
        "headingId": 1089,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> luteinized thecomatosis associated with sclerosing peritonitis.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T10:14:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1074,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 1090,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 152562,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 155,
        "headingId": 1090,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T10:14:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1075,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 1091,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 152563,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 155,
        "headingId": 1091,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These tumours are localized in the ovary; when small, they may be confined to the ovarian cortex.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T10:14:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1076,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 1092,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 152564,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 155,
        "headingId": 1092,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Luteinized thecoma associated with sclerosing peritonitis is almost always bilateral, although one ovary may be substantially smaller than the other. Patients usually present with abdominal swelling, pain, ascites, and symptoms of bowel obstruction. These symptoms are secondary to sclerosing peritonitis, which is nearly universal but may be subclinical and subtle. Hormonal manifestations are usually absent {18636018; 8279621; 33053314}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T10:14:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1077,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 1093,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 152565,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 155,
        "headingId": 1093,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>This is an extremely rare lesion. In the largest reported series, these neoplasms occurred over a wide age range (10&nbsp;months to 85&nbsp;years) but most commonly in young women (median age: 28&nbsp;years) {18636018}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T10:14:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1078,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 1094,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 152566,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 155,
        "headingId": 1094,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T10:14:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1079,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 1095,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 152567,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 155,
        "headingId": 1095,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Bilaterality, predominant cortical involvement in some cases, and envelopment (rather than obliteration) of pre-existing ovarian structures suggest a non-neoplastic process in at least some cases {18636018}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T10:14:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1086,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 1102,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 152568,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 155,
        "headingId": 1102,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Both ovaries are usually involved, although the degree of ovarian enlargement varies. The ovaries are usually soft and sometimes cerebriform, with a tan to red sectioned surface.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T10:14:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1080,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 1096,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 152569,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 155,
        "headingId": 1096,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The ovaries are hypercellular, usually with scattered, often conspicuous zones of oedema, sometimes imparting a microcystic appearance. The cells are predominantly spindled and are bland but often exhibit brisk mitotic activity. A minority of the cells are rounded, with pale or eosinophilic cytoplasm, representing luteinized or weakly luteinized cells. Entrapment of ovarian follicles and diffuse involvement of the cortex with sparing of the medulla may be conspicuous, especially when the ovaries are only mildly enlarged. The spindle cells are usually negative for inhibin and calretinin but positive for SF1 and FOXL2, whereas the luteinized cells are positive for inhibin and calretinin {18636018; 24076780}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T10:14:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1081,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 1097,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 152570,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 155,
        "headingId": 1097,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T10:14:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1082,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 1098,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 152571,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 155,
        "headingId": 1098,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T10:14:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1085,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 1101,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 152572,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 155,
        "headingId": 1101,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential: </em>bilateral cellular spindle cell proliferation with luteinized or weakly luteinized cells.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T10:14:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1083,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 1099,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 152573,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 155,
        "headingId": 1099,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These are benign neoplasms and are not staged.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T10:14:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1084,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 1100,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 152574,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 155,
        "headingId": 1100,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Several patients have died of complications related to intestinal obstruction due to the sclerosing peritonitis, but there has been no recurrence or metastasis of the ovarian lesion {18636018}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T10:14:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]